WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
- Is it true that you,

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.270
you were once in a stage
version- I love this,

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.070
of "Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure"?

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.530
- Yeah, that was the play we did

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.852
in my senior year of high school.

00:00:08.852 --> 00:00:11.045
- I love that this is a play.
- This is cool.

00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:12.270
- Oh yeah.
- I know.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.310
I, ours were like, I mean, they were fine

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.620
but they were the classic
ones everybody always does.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.420
I just thought that was
very progressive and cool.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.040
- Oh, well it was,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.850
I didn't take the drama
class, but the kids who did,

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.460
their assignment was to write this play,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.237
and adapt a play, and they chose

00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:30.600
"Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure."

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.073
And so one of my,

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.877
friends from football and
rugby, M.C., he was like,

00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:38.340
"Yeah, like I'm writing it.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.290
Come audition to be Bill and like

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.030
let's audition together as Bill and Ted."

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.260
And we did and we both got it.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.705
- Oh my gosh.
- That is so fun.

00:00:44.705 --> 00:00:45.713
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
(audience applauds)

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:48.090
- It was a lot of fun.
- I, no, this is not a joke.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.829
I literally learned
certain historical figures

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:54.270
(Amy laughs)
- from that movie.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:55.870
- We'll take education
wherever we can get it.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.050
- I was like, look,

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.688
before Hamilton came around

00:00:58.688 --> 00:01:00.300
I was learning from Bill and Ted. (laughs)

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.140
- Yep.
- [Gabriel] Oh yeah.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:01.973
- Socrates.

00:01:01.973 --> 00:01:02.806
- It's entertaining,

00:01:02.806 --> 00:01:04.500
and something historical
you're learning about.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.613
So what's the strangest
play you've ever done?

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:09.270
- Ooh, wow. God that's a good question.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.879
I feel like I was a snow,
like a, a snowflake.

00:01:11.879 --> 00:01:12.960
- Oh, wow.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.550
- In like in second or third grade.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.960
And she didn't really have an arc.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.580
We don't, we don't know
what her character was.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.710
It was, it was, it was a mess.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.090
- Well hey, there are no small parts.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.740
There's only small actors.
- That's right.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.090
- Oh, okay, I like that.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.190
Is that a thing people
say? I've never heard that?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.720
- [Amy] Yeah.
- Oh, I'm not an actor.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.227
- They usually say it to the
people that have small parts.

00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:33.422
(Kelly, Gabriel, and Amy laughing)

